  "live_records": {
    "q-36354": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36354",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & =2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & c & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=4,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
