    },
    "q-35793": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35793",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  .",
      "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 9-(-5)\\cdot (-6)}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
